Jump to the specific time specified by the parameter
of ffrGotoXTag(). The specified time might have or have not
value change; if it has value change, then the return time
is exactly the same as the specified time; if it has not
value change, then the return time is aligned forward
(toward smaller time direction).
There is an exception for the jump alignment: If the
specified time is smaller than the minimum time where has
value changes, then the return time is aligned to the
minimum time.
if (FSDB_RC_SUCCESS != vc_trvs_hdl
- >ffrGotoXTag((void*)&time)) {
