Signal-Based Scheme
To create value change by signal based scheme, the application traverses and creates all
the value changes of a variable. Then it rewinds the time and performs the same routines
on another variable. Here is the example code to demonstrate signal-based value change
creation:
struct MySignal _sig;
fsdbTag64 xtag;
unsigned char val;
xtag.H = 0; xtag.L = 5;
val = (unsigned char) FSDB_BT_VCD_0;
xtag.L = 23;
val = (unsigned char) FSDB_BT_VCD_1;
ffw_ResetXCoor(obj);
xtag.H = 0; xtag.L = 5;
val = (unsigned char) FSDB_BT_VCD_Z;
xtag.L = 17;
val = (unsigned char) FSDB_BT_VCD_X;
xtag.L = 23;
val = (unsigned char) FSDB_BT_VCD_1;

The above example code traverses and creates all the value changes of the circle variable
(time 5: value 0, time 32: value 1), then it rewinds the time (by calling ffw_ResetXCoor).
After that, similar steps are performed on the triangle variable. The application should
