npi_objects_overlap
Check if two handles overlap physically.
The NPI routine npi_objects_overlap() returns 1 (TRUE) if the two handles overlap
physically.
Otherwise, it returns 0 (FALSE).
Valid input handles belong to vh name, simple expression, part-select, or indexed partselect.
If any input handle does not belong to these types, npi_objects_overlap always returns 0
(FALSE).
VC Apps NPI treats a non-constant variable as an arbitrary value.

reg [2:0] pr;
integer i = 0;
npi_objects_overlap (pr[1:0], pr[p]); // return 1
npi_objects_overlap (pr[1:0], pr[i]); // return 1; It is possible to
be overlapped because VC Apps NPI cannot get its value (defined in
simulation time), treats "i" as arbitrary value.
npi_objects_overlap (pr[i:1], pr[p]); // return 0; It is impossible to be
overlapped even if VC Apps NPI treats "i" as arbitrary value.

The following is another example:
struct packed {
reg [0:7] b;
npi_compare_objects (ps[8:4], ps.b[0:1]); // return 1

