npi_dm_create_range
Create a range object, such as [1:0] in SystemVerilog HDL. If this function is called
multiple times with the same left range and right range, it reuses and return the
object previously created.

npiDmHandle npi_dm_create_range( NPI_INT32 left, NPI_INT32 right );
npiDmHandle npi_dm_create_range( npiDmHandle left, npiDmHandle right );

This argument specifies the left boundary of the created range object.

This argument specifies the right boundary of the created range object.
On success, the range handle is returned.

{
//-- DM operation -----------------------------------------npiDmHandle range_hdl1 = npi_dm_create_range( 7, 0 );
npiDmHandle range_hdl2 = npi_dm_create_range( 7, 0 );
if ( range_hdl1 == range_hdl2 )
printf( "range_hdl1 and range_hdl2 are the same object.\n" );
// Use handle as range input
npiDmHandle c3 = npi_dm_create_constant( 3 );
npiDmHandle c0 = npi_dm_create_constant( 0 );
npiDmHandle range_hdl3 = npi_dm_create_range( c3, c0 );

}

range_hdl1 and range_hdl2 are the same object.

Tcl
npi_dm_create_range -left LeftRange -right RightRange [-int | -handle]

-left LeftRange

This argument specifies the left boundary of the created range object.
-right RightRange

This argument specifies the right boundary of the created range object.
-int | -handle

This argument specifies the type of boundary input. Specify the input type is integer by
-int. Specify the input type is npiDmHandle by -handle. This parameter is optional. The
default is -int.
On success, the range handle is returned.

set range_hdl1 [npi_dm_create_range -left 7 -right 0]
set range_hdl2 [npi_dm_create_range -left 7 -right 0]
if { [string equal $range_hdl1 $range_hdl2] } {
puts "range_hdl1 and range_hdl2 are the same object."
}
Use handle as range input
set c3 [npi_dm_create_constant -value 3]
set c0 [npi_dm_create_constant -value 0]
set range_hdl3 [npi_dm_create_range -left $c3 -right $c0 -handle]

range_hdl1 and range_hdl2 are the same object.

